  "term": "asceticism",
  "definition": "Asceticism is a way of life that tries to achieve moral or spiritual aims through strict restraint of bodily appetites and worldly desires. It is presented less as a theory than as a practical discipline based on the view that a higher good stands in opposition to ordinary impulse and earthly interests.",
